{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c503","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07962-00f2-7aa3-bdba-fd54caa2b073"},"sequence":220,"recorded_at":1780531400000435,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0e106057-555a-4629-8228-1b6dea88eaef","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0e106057-555a-4629-8228-1b6dea88eaef","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0e106057-555a-4629-8228-1b6dea88eaef"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"3f611f06-41de-47b3-8557-9a8ee23c76c1"},"task_id":"3f611f06-41de-47b3-8557-9a8ee23c76c1","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"3f611f06-41de-47b3-8557-9a8ee23c76c1","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-10-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board q 'get(TASK-260906-vmzk0y) { full }' --format json 2>&1 | python3 -c \\\"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(json.dumps(d, indent=1)[:9000])\\\"\",\n  \"description\": \"Dump full task record\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\n \\\"ac\\\": \\\"Production behavior demonstrates: the Provider Protocol 3.0.0 envelope has exactly one named owner, recorded in provhost stated bounds and the ownership registry, with either working v3 admission or an explicit stated bound naming the deferring task; a v3 envelope reaching provhost produces the documented outcome under test in both directions. A provider discovery failure lifts into an axerror Structured Error through a production path that axerror accepts, proven by a test driving the real lift and a negative test showing a causal-leak shape is refused. No machine-local path is echoed into any wire message.\\\",\\n \\\"assignee\\\": \\\"[implementer] developer (muse)\\\",\\n \\\"blockedBy\\\": [\\n  \\\"TASK-260906-3pln7q\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"blocks\\\": [\\n  \\\"TASK-260906-v8heil\\\"\\n ],\\n \\\"checklist\\\": [\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Provider Protocol 3.0.0 envelope has exactly one named owner, recorded in provhost stated bounds and the traceability ownership registry\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"A v3 envelope reaching provhost produces the documented outcome, driven in both directions: admitted where the owner accepts it and refused with the named arm where it does not\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"The Error 1.3.0 binding for v3 is either implemented or an explicit stated bound names the deferring task; protocol.go no longer binds major 2 to Error 1.0.0 silently for v3\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"A provider discovery failure lifts into an axerror Structured Error through a production path that axerror accepts, proven by driving the real lift\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"A negative test shows a causal-leak shape is refused; no machine-local path, provider ID or owner identity reaches any wire message\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"CheckProviderDescriptor is completed or relocated to the named owner, and the traceability registry records which package owns 7.A\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Every census or roster derives its denominator from production and fails closed on an unregistered site, an orphan row, an import alias and a var-binding, each control-planted\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Mutation battery reports killed over applied on a production-derived denominator with narrowing, arm-deletion and census-only separate, and NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL as distinct rows\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Candidate tree OID in the outcome document equals the one the Change Request record carries, verified by listing the tree\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Code written per task description and AC\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio \\\\u2014 `n of m AC rows driven` \\\\u2014 and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant \\\\u2014 the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Lint clean\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Implementation matches AC\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Solution fits project architecture\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Tests green\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Gate, refusal, validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read \\\\u2014 positive-path-only evidence is not accepted\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"If review does not accept the work \\\\u2014 verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  }\\n ],\\n \\\"children\\\": [],\\n \\\"created\\\": \\\"2026-09-06T07:18:55Z\\\",\\n \\\"derivedBlockedBy\\\": [],\\n \\\"derivedBlocks\\\": [],\\n \\\"description\\\": \\\"Close advisories A3 and A4. A3: catalog pins every provider operation to contract versions 2.0.0 and 3.0.0 with normative section 7.2/7.5/7.A (catalog_gen.go:190-204), but provhost pins ProtocolMajor=2 (protocol.go:30), classifies every 3.x envelope as incompatible_protocol (protocol.go:449), binds Structured Error 1.0.0 only (protocol.go:381), and its stated-bounds paragraph never mentions v3; the only 7.A production code is terminalbackend.CheckProviderDescriptor, which provhost cannot call. Name the owner of the v3 envelope and its Error 1.3.0 binding, record it in provhost stated bounds and the ownership registry, and complete or relocate CheckProviderDescriptor accordingly. A4: internal/provider mints errors whose detail embeds canonical filesystem paths, provider IDs, and owner identities and whose Error() appends the cause (provider.go:77-97, trustCandidate, Verify); axerror.refuseCausalLeak (details.go:202-215) will refuse a wire message built from it, so the seam cannot compose when cmd/ax lifts a discovery failure. Restructure provider constructors onto the provhost details-map pattern, or record the composition contract in the package doc.\\\",\\n \\\"estimate\\\": {\\n  \\\"kind\\\": \\\"estimated\\\",\\n  \\\"scale\\\"