{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d05b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07962-00f2-7aa3-bdba-fd54caa2b073"},"sequence":1672,"recorded_at":1780531400003339,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0e106057-555a-4629-8228-1b6dea88eaef","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"0e106057-555a-4629-8228-1b6dea88eaef","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0e106057-555a-4629-8228-1b6dea88eaef"},"call_id":"call_01a07973d71e78c08a0396b1310ef7c4","text":"Read text file `/tmp/r6rev/outcome-round5.md`.\n1|# TASK-260906-vmzk0y — own-provider-protocol-v3-envelope-and-error-lift (round 5)\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review (handed off to review; board status `to-review`).\n4|\n5|Candidate tree: `d6253f58fe72a84c0900329c686300f232374874`\n6|(verified by `git ls-tree -r`: all six new files\n7|`internal/provider/lift.go`, `internal/provider/lift_test.go`,\n8|`internal/terminalbackend/descriptor.go`,\n9|`internal/terminalbackend/descriptor_test.go`,\n10|`internal/terminalbackend/semver_major_edge_test.go`,\n11|`internal/terminalbackend/digit_range_census_test.go` are in-tree;\n12|`git hash-object` of the worktree `semver_major_edge_test.go`,\n13|`digit_range_census_test.go`, `descriptor_test.go`, and `LOGBOOK.md`\n14|byte-for-byte equals the tree blobs. Built via a detached index —\n15|`GIT_INDEX_FILE` copy + `read-tree HEAD` + `add -A` + `write-tree` — so\n16|the worktree index is untouched.)\n17|\n18|Round 5 answers review-verdict-rev4: two blocking findings (F1\n19|`semverMajor` saturation guard pinned only far from its edge, F2\n20|`descriptorGeometry` digit gate with no witness in the upper half of its\n21|rejected class — third consecutive round of one class, both sites inside\n22|this leaf's delta) plus the standing census item. Everything else stands\n23|exactly as the reviewer verified it in rev4 — G-A (derived\n24|behavioural-versus-census split), G-B (provhost saturation edge and\n25|`/`/`:` digit boundaries), §7.A ownership, v3 envelope both directions,\n26|the lift seam, N6 — and is not re-litigated here. No production change\n27|in round 5: the `semverMajor` guard and the `descriptorGeometry` gate\n28|were already correct; the delta is two new test files, two `1E2` rows in\n29|the value-refusals table, and the logbook entry.\n30|\n31|## F1 (blocking, closed) — semverMajor saturation guard pinned at its edge\n32|\n33|The guard `major > (math.MaxInt-digit)/10`\n34|(`internal/terminalbackend/terminalbackend.go:258`) was witnessed only\n35|by literals that saturate under the weakened guard too\n36|(`18446744073709551617` → MaxInt, `9223372036854775808` → −2^63, both\n37|still `!= 1`, still refused). The true narrowing\n38|`major > math.MaxInt/10` (S1, drops the `digit` term — the exact M3/F1a\n39|shape) survived the whole terminalbackend suite and admits\n40|`922337203685477580801.0.0` at `ParseProviderDescriptor` with `err =\n41|nil` (semverMajor returns 1, aliasing native major 1). The aliasing\n42|reaches every `semverMajor(...) != 1` site: `New`/`RegisterExternal`\n43|(`terminalbackend.go:235`), `CheckVersionTuple` (`:556`),\n44|`manifest.go:1072/1155/1301`, `descriptor.go:168`.\n45|\n46|New `TestSemverMajorSaturationEdge` (internal, mirroring\n47|`TestParseMajorSaturationEdge`) drives five rows — largest exact fit\n48|`9223372036854775807.0.0`, first saturated `9223372036854775808.0.0`,\n49|and the aliasing witness `922337203685477580801.0.0` with its ±1\n50|neighbours `...800`/`...802` — each requiring semverMajor == MaxInt\n51|(not merely refusal: the neighbours refuse under S1 too, so the value\n52|pin carries those kills) AND refusal with the named arm at the\n53|production entries: `descriptor protocol version` at\n54|`ParseProviderDescriptor`, `protocol_version major 1` at\n55|`CheckVersionTuple` (list carries the version itself, so only the major\n56|arm can refuse), and the witness at `New` (`protocol_versions major\n57|1`). Controls pin `1.0.0 → 1`, `2.0.0 → 2`, and the old-corpus witness\n58|still saturating (documenting the blind region it lived in).\n59|\n60|| `protocol_version` | shipped | under S1 (`> MaxInt/10`) |\n61||---|---|---|\n62|| `9223372036854775807.0.0` (MaxInt, largest exact fit) | (MaxInt, refuse) | identical (exact fit, no saturation) |\n63|| `9223372036854775808.0.0` (MaxInt+1, first saturated) | (MaxInt, refuse) | (−2^63, refuse — exit same, value kills) |\n64|| `922337203685477580800.0.0` (neighbour, wraps to 0) | (MaxInt, refuse) | (0, refuse — value kills) |\n65|| `922337203685477580801.0.0` (aliasing witness, wraps to 1) | (MaxInt, refuse) | (1, ADMITTED err=nil — entry kills) |\n66|| `922337203685477580802.0.0` (neighbour, wraps to 2) | (MaxInt, refuse) | (2, refuse — value kills) |\n67|\n68|Witness construction: `922337203685477580` walks the accumulator to\n69|exactly MaxInt/10; the next `8` overflows int64 to −2^63; the following\n70|`0` multiplies by 10 (0 mod 2^64), resetting to 0; the final digit lands\n71|on 0/1/2. Measured: S1 is KILLED by `TestSemverMajorSaturationEdge`\n72|alone (`semverMajor(\"9223372036854775808.0.0\") = -9223372036854775808,\n73|want saturation to math.MaxInt`), with zero census kill (census mask\n74|exit 0, 2 RUN / 2 PASS, verified non-empty).\n75|\n76|## F2 (blocking, closed) — geometry digit gate witnessed at its true edge\n77|\n78|The gate `digit < '0' || digit > '9'`\n79|(`internal/terminalbackend/descriptor.go:235`) was witnessed at `e`\n80|(0x65) at best — 44 bytes above the true edge `9` (0x39). Every mutant\n81|upper bound X with `E <= X < e` admits uppercase `E` and survived. Under\n82|D2 (`digit > 'E'`), `columns: 1E2` — a valid JSON number naming 100 —\n83|is admitted as Columns = 312 (`1`, then `E` valued at 0x45−0x30 = 21,\n84|then `2`; 1·10+21 = 31, 31·10+2 = 312): a fabricated in-range value.\n85|\n86|Two `1E2` rows added to `TestParseProviderDescriptorValueRefusals`\n87|(columns and rows, asserting `descriptor geometry digits`); the rows row\n88|proves the fix is at the shared gate, not at one call. Measured: D2 and\n89|the token-preserving D1 (`if digit == 'E' { continue }`, condition text\n90|byte-identical) are both KILLED by the new rows alone, with zero census\n91|kill (census mask exit 0, 2 RUN / 2 PASS, verified non-empty).\n92|\n93|## Item 3 — census of all three digit-range comparisons (recorded)\n94|\n95|`internal/terminalbackend/digit_range_census_test.go` carries the file\n96|header census; each row below names the committed witness that makes\n97|\"covered\" checkable instead of asserted:\n98|\n99|| Site | Condition | Reachable rejected class (domain) | Adjacent witnesses | Declared equivalents |\n100||---|---|---|---|---|\n101|| provhost parseMajor major arm (`protocol.go:379`) | `digit < '0' \\|\\| digit > '9'` | every non-digit byte (JSON string) | `/` (0x2F), `:` (0x3A) in `TestParseMajorDigitBoundariesRefuseAtEntry` | letters/signs in the older corpus |\n102|| provhost parseMajor rest arm (`protocol.go:397`) | `rest[i] < '0' \\|\\| rest[i] > '9'` | same | `/`/`:` in minor AND patch positions, same test | rest letters (control rows) |\n103|| terminalbackend descriptorGeometry (`descriptor.go:235`) | `digit < '0' \\|\\| digit > '9'` | exactly `{-, +, ., e, E}` (json.Number) | `-` (`-80`/`-24`), `.` (`80.0`/`24.5`), `e` (`1e2`), `E` (`1E2`, this round) on both members | `+`: one line, not a row (N9) — only legal after e/E, which refuses first; `/`/`:` provably unreachable (see below) |\n104|\n105|`TestDescriptorGeometryAdjacentsNeverReachTheGate` proves the `/`-`:`\n106|unreachability claim executably: `1/2` and `1:2` on both members are\n107|refused with the document syntax mismatch arm before the gate runs — the\n108|inverse of the provhost rows, which is why the same adjacent characters\n109|need opposite tests at the two domains. Deliberately out of scope (one\n110|line in the header, not an oversight): the hex three-way splits in\n111|`manifest.go`/`surrogate.go` predate this leaf and are a different\n112|shape; the two saturation guards are accumulation bounds pinned by the\n113|edge tests, not by adjacent characters.\n114|\n115|## Round-5 mutation battery (F1/F2 gates + re-pinned census sites)\n116|\n117|Denominator re-derived from production to cover the gates under review\n118|rather than provhost alone: the three digit-range comparisons above\n119|plus both saturation guards. Harness\n120|`TASK-260906-vmzk0y_mut-round5.py` (spec\n121|`TASK-260906-vmzk0y_spec-round5.json`, results\n122|`TASK-260906-vmzk0y_battery-round5.json`, all attached); mutants applied\n123|to a scratch copy at `/tmp/vmzk0y-rev5-mut`, never to the candidate\n124|worktree (`ALL RESTORED`, SHA-256 asserted per file; worktree `git\n125|status` confirms only the intended delta). Every `go test` ran as a\n126|standalone process with its real exit code preserved (no pipe chain).\n127|Killer split: BEHAVIOURAL = drives a production entry point;\n128|CENSUS = source-text inventory only\n129|(`TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllWitnessed` /\n130|`TestWitnessedArmsAreAllDerived` in provhost,\n131|`TestDerivedRefusalArmsAreAllDeclared` /\n132|`TestDeclaredRefusalArmsAreAllDerived` in terminalbackend). Every mask\n133|verified non-empty (census 2 RUN, behavioural ≥1 RUN).\n134|\n135|Applied 9 / killed 8 / survived 1 (declared equivalent, bound below).\n136|Controls NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL are distinct rows, not counted as\n137|applied.\n138|\n139|| Mutant | What it narrows the gate to | Named test(s) that fail | Killer |\n140||---|---|---|---|\n141|| P-M3 narrowing (provhost saturation): `> (MaxInt-step)/10` → `> MaxInt/10` | threshold off by one; `...802` aliases native 2 | `TestParseMajorSaturationEdge` | BEHAVIOURAL (census exit 0) |\n142|| P-M6 narrowing (major digit arm): `digit > ':'` | major admits exactly `:` | `TestParseMajorDigitBoundariesRefuseAtEntry` + census pair | BOTH |\n143|| P-M17 narrowing/token-preserving: insert `if digit == ':' { continue }` | major admits exactly `:`; census byte-identical | `TestParseMajorDigitBoundariesRefuseAtEntry` | BEHAVIOURAL ONLY (census exit 0 — the point) |\n144|| T-S1 TRUE NARROWING (semverMajor saturation): `> (MaxInt-digit)/10` → `> MaxInt/10` | threshold off by one; `...801` aliases native 1 and is admitted | `TestSemverMajorSaturationEdge` | BEHAVIOURAL (census exit 0) |\n145|| T-S2 delete-shaped (saturation): guard → `> math.MaxInt` (never fires) | accumulation wraps again; proves the gate exists, not its edge | `TestParseProviderDescriptorProtocolVersionOverflowVectors`, `TestSemverMajorSaturationEdge` | BEHAVIOURAL (census exit 0) |\n146|| T-D1 narrowing/token-preserving: insert `if digit == 'E' { continue }` | geometry admits exactly `E`; census byte-identical | `TestParseProviderDescriptorValueRefusals` (+`columns_exponent_uppercase`, +`rows_exponent_uppercase`) | BEHAVIOURAL ONLY (census exit 0 — the point) |\n147|| T-D2 narrowing (geometry bound shift): `digit > 'E'` | geometry admits `:`–`E`; `1E2` admitted as 312 | same rows | BEHAVIOURAL (census exit 0) |\n148|| T-D3 narrowing/token-preserving: insert `if digit == '+' { continue }` | no reachable disposition changes | SURVIVES — declared equivalent, bound below | survivor bound stated |\n149|| T-D4 arm-deletion: geometry digit-gate block deleted | non-digits fall to the bound arm or accumulate; digits arm gone | `TestParseProviderDescriptorValueRefusals` (+7 subrows) + census pair | BOTH (census co-fires by construction — the arm is removed) |\n150|\n151|Class split: narrowing 4/4 killed (incl. the true semverMajor narrowing\n152|T-S1); narrowing/token-preserving 2/3 killed-or-equivalent (P-M17, T-D1\n153|killed behaviourally with zero census kill; T-D3 equivalent);\n154|delete-shaped 1/1 killed; arm-deletion 1/1 killed; equivalence 0/1\n155|(declared equivalent).\n156|\n157|Distinct control rows, NOT counted as applied mutants:\n158|\n159|| Control | Disposition |\n160||---|---|\n161|| X1: anchor `>= math.MaxInt` absent from source (0 sites) | NOT_APPLIED |\n162|| X2: saturation block deleted outright (`math` import unused) | COMPILE_FAIL |\n163|\n164|Survival bound: T-D3 survives because `+` is only legal in a\n165|json.Number after `e`/`E`, which the unchanged gate refuses first, so\n166|the mutant changes no disposition on any reachable literal (full suite\n167|461/461 green under it, behavioural mask 28/28 green). A lower-bound\n168|narrowing admitting `+` admits `-` too (0x2B < 0x2D), which the `-80`\n169|row kills — so `+` adds no narrowing power and gets the declared line,\n170|not a row (N9). Recorded in the census header so it is not mistaken for\n171|a hole later.\n172|\n173|Per-arm verdict: every gate under review now carries at least one\n174|BEHAVIOURAL killer. The two token-preserving narrowings that the\n175|inventory is blind to by construction (P-M17, T-D1) carry a behavioural\n176|killer and explicitly no census kill.\n177|\n178|## Notes N4/N6/N7\n179|\n180|- N4 (carried): the `foreignMajor` peek widening placement outside this\n181|  delta was accepted in round 3; this round touches no production file\n182|  at all (`git diff HEAD --name-only` shows only prior-round paths plus\n183|  the two new test files and the `descriptor_test.go`/`LOGBOOK.md`\n184|  edits), so the placement still holds by construction.\n185|- N6 (carried): the N2 CallExpr-only bound sits on\n186|  `TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding`'s doc comment;\n187|  untouched this round.\n188|- N7 (carried): the §7.A deferral still names no follow-up board item —\n189|  per the round-4 brief this is the orchestrator's board-element freeze,\n190|  not a producer omission.\n191|\n192|## AC row coverage: 14 of 15 driven + 1 stated bound (carried)\n193|\n194|Rows 1–5 and 7–13 were driven through the production entry point by the\n195|named test in rounds 1–3 and re-run green in this round's full suite\n196|(exit 0, 22 pkgs, 0 FAIL); rows 6 and 15 gain the round-5 rows below;\n197|row 14 stays a stated bound.\n198|\n199|| # | AC / DoD row | Production call site | Driving test / bound |\n200||---|---|---|---|\n201|| 1 | v3 envelope has exactly one named owner, recorded in provhost stated bounds and the ownership registry | `internal/provhost/doc.go`, `ownership.v0.5.0.json` `section:7.A` | `tracecheck`: ok (60 contracts, 36 sections, 98 cases) |\n202|| 2 | working v3 admission or explicit stated bound naming the deferral | `terminalbackend.AdmitProviderDescriptor`; `provhost/doc.go` | `TestAdmitProviderDescriptorAdmitsMatchingBinding`, `TestAdmitProviderDescriptorRefusesMismatch` |\n203|| 3 | v3 envelope reaching provhost → documented outcome, both directions | `provhost.DecodeResponse`; `terminalbackend.AdmitProviderDescriptor` | `TestDecodeResponseWellFormedV3SuccessIsMismatch`, `TestDecodeResponseV3FailureWithValid130ErrorIsMismatch` |\n204|| 4 | Error 1.3.0 binding implemented-or-deferred; no silent major-2 binding for v3 | `provhost.DecodeResponse` (observed-major contract), `axerror.BindingFor`/`DecodeBound` | `TestDecodeResponseV2FailureWith130ErrorIsBoundTo100`; the v3 test decodes its embedded error through production `(provider, 3)` → 1.3.0 |\n205|| 5 | F1 (rev1): geometry bound decided on digits, overflow refused | `terminalbackend.descriptorGeometry` | `TestParseProviderDescriptorGeometryOverflowVectors` |\n206|| 6 | majors never wrap; saturation validates the full shape; guard edges, digit edges, and the three-site census pinned | `terminalbackend.semverMajor`, `provhost.parseMajor` + `DecodeResponse`, `terminalbackend.descriptorGeometry` | prior rows (round 4) + NEW `TestSemverMajorSaturationEdge` (T-S1/T-S2), NEW `1E2` value-refusal rows (T-D1/T-D2), NEW `TestDescriptorGeometryAdjacentsNeverReachTheGate` + census header (item 3) |\n207|| 7 | F4: registered-but-unlifted code produces no wire object | `provider.Lift` | `TestLiftRefusesRegisteredCodeWithoutLiftArm`, `TestLiftRefusesUnregisteredCode` |\n208|| 8 | discovery failure lifts into an axerror Structured Error through an accepted production path | `provider.Lift` | `TestLiftCarriesDiscoveryFailuresToTheWire` |\n209|| 9 | causal-leak shape refused (negative) | `axerror.New` | `TestNaiveLiftShapeIsRefusedByTheWireGate` |\n210|| 10 | no machine-local path, provider ID, or owner identity on any wire message | `provider.Lift`, `terminalbackend` parse arms | wire-absence asserts in all 4 lift vectors; `TestParseProviderDescriptorRefusesWithoutEchoingLocalData` |\n211|| 11 | CheckProviderDescriptor completed; registry owns 7.A | `terminalbackend.ParseProviderDescriptor` + `AdmitProviderDescriptor`; registry | inventory bijection (terminalbackend) + rows; `tracecheck` ok |\n212|| 12 | F3: bound rests on true facts, both halves pinned | `provhost/identity.go` header | `TestSpecIdentityExampleVerifiesAgainstItsClaimedDigest`, `TestNoProductionPathAttestsProviderIdentityBinding` |\n213|| 13 | F5: census derives the whole package, every form, fail-closed | `loadProviderCodes` | `TestLiftCoversTheClosedCodeSet` + plants |\n214|| 14 | F6: future caller recorded | `terminalbackend/descriptor.go` | STATED BOUND (prose by nature; names path, order, two miswirings) |\n215|| 15 | mutation battery with narrowing / token-preserving / arm-deletion / census-only split | `/tmp` harness (attached) | this round: 9 applied / 8 killed / 1 survived-equivalent + NOT_APPLIED + COMPILE_FAIL distinct; prior batteries stand |\n216|\n217|## Production changes in round 5 (none)\n218|\n219|- `internal/terminalbackend/semver_major_edge_test.go` (new):\n220|  `TestSemverMajorSaturationEdge`.\n221|- `internal/terminalbackend/digit_range_census_test.go` (new): three-site\n222|  census record + `TestDescriptorGeometryAdjacentsNeverReachTheGate`.\n223|- `internal/terminalbackend/descriptor_test.go`: two `1E2` rows.\n224|- `LOGBOOK.md`: entry 2254 (this round).\n225|- All other paths byte-identical to rev4; leaf-1 packages untouched.\n226|\n227|## Gates re-run by this round (nothing accepted from prior rounds)\n228|\n229|| Gate | Result |\n230||---|---|\n231|| `go build ./...` | exit 0 |\n232|| `go vet ./...` | exit 0 |\n233|| `gofmt -l internal/` | clean |\n234|| `go test ./... -count=1` | exit 0, 22 packages ok, 0 FAIL |\n235|| `go test ./internal/terminalbackend/ ./internal/provhost/ ./internal/provider/ -cover -count=1` | exit 0 — 94.2% / 85.8% / 97.8% |\n236|| `go test -race ./internal/terminalbackend/ ./internal/provhost/ -count=1` | exit 0 (both) |\n237|| `GOOS=windows go build ./...` | exit 0 |\n238|| `GOOS=windows go vet` (three touched packages) | exit 0 |\n239|| `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` | ok — contracts=60, normative_sections=36, acceptance_cases=98 |\n240|| terminalbackend refusal-arm bijection | unchanged rows, suite green (no new production arm) |","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
