s Session Adapter Probe 7.8) — selection is by a structural fragment only the Session Adapter sentence carries, and the parse still covers the whole sentence; member sentences contain digit-period-digit abbreviations (`Section 7.5`, `Structured Error 1.1`), so the sentence scanner skips those; unions use three pipe encodings (`\\\\|` in the operation table, raw `|` in prose, `&#124;` in the manifest table); the manifest table pairs members per row (`schema`/`schema_version` etc.), so the first cell contributes every bare snake_case span; the `probe` row name recurs in four tables, so row unions are windowed to the 7.8 registry table; fidelity profiles come from the `projection-plan` operation row (4 values — the 13.14 `Profiles are` sentence lists 5 including `archive_only`, which is a strategy there, never a profile).\\n- REFACTOR (production-first, same `var` + `validX` loop idiom the package already uses): `capabilityStatuses`/`validCapabilityStatus` (probe.go), `readPurposes`/`validReadPurpose` and `findingSeverities`/`validFindingSeverity` (context.go), `tupleArchitectures`/`validTupleArchitecture` (tuple.go); the four inline-literal checks now loop the tables. Roles, directions, candidate kinds, and platforms derive from the existing `Role`/`Direction`/`CandidateKind`/`scalar.Platform` consts with no production change (tuple platforms delegate to `scalar.ParsePlatform`).\\n- TEST: new `TestDecodeProbeClosedRules/bad_status` — no behavioral test refused a fifth status, so a `return true` mutant of `validCapabilityStatus` survived the suite with the static census green. The mutant is now killed by the entry point (`DecodeProbe`).\\n- EVIDENCE (executed mutants, `/tmp/sessadapter-mutants.sh`, tree verified identical before/after): M1 `capabilityStatuses`+`bogus` killed by `TestValueVocabulariesMatchSpec`; M2 `findingSeverities`+`fatal` killed by `TestDecodeFindingRules/bad_severity`; M3 `requestMembers`+`zzz` killed by `TestClosedMemberSetsAreDerivedFromSpec/request_envelope`; M4 `validCapabilityStatus`→`return true` (all searched-for tokens preserved) leaves the static census green and is killed by the behavioral suite (`TestDecodeProbeClosedRules/bad_status`); M5 unregistered vocabulary-shaped `var` killed by `TestClosedVocabularyTablesAreRegistered`. 8/8 as required, 0 survived.\\n- TRACEABILITY: 7 acceptance cases appended (`session-adapter-discovery/-manifest/-probe/-operations/-limits/-idempotency/-tuple-gates`, each bound to one production declaration and its named positive/refusal tests), digest re-pinned to `78d9bc9b...`, count pins 81->88, README ownership paragraph 81->88 plus a sessadapter disclosure paragraph that keeps the Section 7.8 clause-level binding `unevidenced` (no clause enumerated — no clause-level claim made).\\n- NOTE (pre-existing, not touched): README still says \\\"One admitted binding out of forty-nine\\\" while `tracecheck` measures `bindings=53` — stale since before this task (first run here already showed 53). Flagged for the review rather than fixed in passing.\\n- SCOPE: `internal/sessadapter/{census_test,probe,context,tuple}.go` + `probe_test.go` (bad status), `internal/traceability/{ownership.v0.5.0.json,traceability.go,traceability_test.go,cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go}`, `README.md`, `LOGBOOK.md` (this entry). Work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2z3se0 round 5: B4/B5 closed as classes by derived denominators, N8 indirection refused\\n- FIX (B8): `bound_census_test.go` rosters all 97 production bound sites (six helpers by member, len guards by shape with values normalized out, DecodeFindings cap instantiations): 82 driven at entries both edges, 15 exempt (4 mechanism, 4 plumbing, 3 equivalent, 5 stated-bound 65536-count rows). `requireStringBounds`/`requireUint53Bounds` wrappers are mechanism rows; the 19 caller sites carry the rows.\\n- FIX (B7): `identity_census_test.go` rosters all 62 `X != Y` gates (mechanical classes excluded) plus a 5-row presence census with structural proof: 54 driven zero-on-exempted-side at exported entries (CheckProbe x6 both sides, seal 8x2, admission key x5 entry+binding sides, binding caller-side x4), 8 exempt (2 dispatch, 4 sentinel, 2 equivalent).\\n- FIX (N8): `constructorSitesInFile` reports any `axerror.New` selector outside call-fun position; synthetic proof covers package-level and function-local indirection (report) vs definition spelling and Decode (exempt).\\n- FINDINGS (battery corrected the work, all in-session): `Bext-min` is genuinely equivalent (no 2-char key satisfies the reverse-DNS grammar); `Iops-candidate` is genuinely equivalent (both sides come from `requireDigestValue`); registry-element gates had no \\\"\\\" row (added `TestRegistryElementEmptyRefuses`); `Ituple-strategies` needed a struct-level [\\\"\\\"] row (added); `Ibind-tuple` first exempted the wrong side (context is never zero; corrected to the admitted side and killed). Len-guard census IDs briefly embedded values and caught a mutant statically — normalized to shape-only so values are pinned behaviorally, per the file's own documented design.\\n- EVIDENCE: battery `/tmp/battery.py`, 153 mutants applied by exact string, PRESENT-confirmed, restore-verified: 147 killed, 6 equivalent-confirmed (3 full-green, 3 behavioral-green with only the roster failing closed on the added clause), 0 survived, 0 not-applied. Additive probe file failed all three censuses naming the planted sites, then removed. Full table attached as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_mutant-table-rev5.md`.\\n- SCOPE: test files only (`bound_census_test.go`, `identity_census_test.go`, `inventory_test.go`, `bounds_edge_test.go`, `zero_absent_test.go`); zero production changes, so no resurrections possible. `go test ./...` 17/17 green, `-cover` green (sessadapter 82.4%), `-race` green on the package, vet + gofmt clean.\\n- STATUS: handed to review, work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2z3se0 round 7: rev6 G-B closed — shape space enumerated per census, three shapes derived, residue bounded\\n- FIX (identity): `identityGatesInSyntax` now derives `bytes.Equal` calls and visits package-level var initializers under their variable name (same scope rule as the constructor census; per-scope ordinals keep all existing rows identical). One live row added: `context.go|CheckContextEcho|bytes.Equal(received.raw, sent.raw)` (domain `context-echo`, driver `TestCheckContextEcho`) — the live instance rev6 named. Header enumerates 8 identity-decision shapes (7 derived, 1 bound: other stdlib predicates) and qualifies the census sentence to derived shapes.\\n- FIX (bound): `boundSitesInSyntax` visits package-level var initializers and derives guards over length variables bound directly from `len(...)`/`stringLength(...)` (parens/conversions unwrap; `values := make(..., len(x))` binds no variable — proven by synthetic negative), plus direct `stringLength(...)` comparisons. Four live mechanism half-rows added (checkStringBounds + checkSortedUniqueStrings enforcements, exempt with caller-row drivers). Header enumerates 10 bound shapes (6 derived, 2 stated-pinned, 2 bounded: decoded-value comparisons with live checkUint53Bounds:269, direct cap/RuneCount with none live) and folds in the 21 refusal-side-only drivers instead of claiming min/max admission per site.\\n- FIX (constructor): no derivation change (7/7 already); header enumerates the 7 construction shapes with residue (frameFault-via-alias, non-Go construction, out-of-dir/_test.go), plus synthetic proofs for failX in return/argument/struct-field positions and returned `axerror.New`.\\n- FINDINGS (battery corrected the work, all in-session): the first length-var rule (RHS subtree contains len) over-derived on `values := make([]T, 0, len(elements))`, claiming element sortedness checks as len sites — tightened to direct binding; the P7 switch-arm plant kills at the arm witness entry, not the switch census (statement-vs-arm division of labor, now stated in the header); capability-clause and mechanism-comparison narrowings always co-fire their census by exact-render design — reported as behavioural kills with expected co-fire, never as clean singles.\\n- EVIDENCE: 15-row battery, 6 behavioural kills (incl. echo same-length narrowing failing `TestCheckContextEcho`, mechanism max+1 failing 5 bound suites, conditional-at-write-gate failing `TestCheckTargetWriteGatesRefusesNonAvailableEnabled`), 6 census-only kills (all three rev6 plant shapes now redden), 3 stated survivors green (plain-param bound, cap, reflect.DeepEqual). Tables attached as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_mutant-table-rev7.md`, narrative as `TASK-260830-2z3se0_rework-evidence-rev7.md`.\\n- SCOPE: test files only (`identity_census_test.go`, `bound_census_test.go`, `inventory_test.go`) + LOGBOOK.md (this entry); zero production changes. `go test ./...` 17/17 green, vet + GOOS=windows vet + gofmt clean, `-race` green, `tracecheck` exit 0 (acceptance_cases=88). Census counts: identity 100 (86/14), bound 107 (80/27), constructors 7; test inventory 109->111 (+2 synthetic, 0 removed).\\n- STATUS: handed to review, work left uncommitted in the worktree for board CR.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 14358,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 3590,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
