{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d24f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a07962-00f2-7aa3-bdba-fd54caa2b073"},"sequence":1922,"recorded_at":1780531400003839,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0e106057-555a-4629-8228-1b6dea88eaef","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0e106057-555a-4629-8228-1b6dea88eaef","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0e106057-555a-4629-8228-1b6dea88eaef"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"03b62daa-5813-4a1b-87fc-7a5cb10dc8c5"},"task_id":"03b62daa-5813-4a1b-87fc-7a5cb10dc8c5","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"03b62daa-5813-4a1b-87fc-7a5cb10dc8c5","chunk":"Read text file `LOGBOOK.md`.\n1|# Flight Logbook\n2|\n3|> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n4|> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n5|\n6|## 2026-09-06\n7|\n8|### 2254 — review round 5: saturation edge carried to semverMajor, geometry upper window closed, three-site digit census recorded (F1/F2)\n9|\n10|- SCOPE: TASK-260906-vmzk0y rework (third consecutive round of the digit-edge class; the two new sites are both inside this leaf's delta in `internal/terminalbackend`). No production change: the `semverMajor` guard and the `descriptorGeometry` gate were already correct. Tests: new `TestSemverMajorSaturationEdge` (largest exact fit 9223372036854775807, +1, aliasing witness 922337203685477580801.0.0 ±1, each requiring semverMajor==MaxInt AND refusal at ParseProviderDescriptor/CheckVersionTuple with the named arm, plus the witness at New); `1E2` rows on columns and rows in the value-refusals table; new `digit_range_census_test.go` recording all three leaf digit-range comparisons with per-site reachable rejected classes and declared equivalents, plus `TestDescriptorGeometryAdjacentsNeverReachTheGate` (`/`/`:` die at document syntax before the gate).\n11|- FINDING (measured): weakened guard `major > math.MaxInt/10` admits 922337203685477580801.0.0 at ParseProviderDescriptor with err=nil (semverMajor returns 1, aliasing native major 1); weakened bound `digit > 'E'` admits `columns: 1E2` as Columns=312; both survived the whole 457-test suite. The neighbours refuse either way, so the value pins (==MaxInt) carry those kills — the round-4 lesson, re-applied. `+` is a declared equivalent (only legal after e/E, which refuses first); `/` and `:` are provably unreachable through json.Number.\n12|- EVIDENCE: outcome `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_outcome-round5.md` on the board task (F1/F2 tables, 9-mutant battery with behavioural-vs-census split per arm, candidate tree OID verified by `ls-tree`); harness `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_mut-round5.py` + `TASK-260906-vmzk0y_battery-round5.json` attached as task resources.\n13|- GATES: `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0 (22 pkgs, 0 FAIL), `-cover` exit 0 (provider 97.8%, provhost 85.8%, terminalbackend 94.2%), `go vet` exit 0, `go build` exit 0, gofmt clean, `tracecheck` ok (60 contracts, 36 sections, 98 cases), `GOOS=windows go build/vet` exit 0, `-race` exit 0 on provhost + terminalbackend. Battery: 9 applied / 8 killed / 1 survived (T-D3 `+`, declared equivalent) + NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL as distinct control rows; the token-preserving narrowings (T-D1 killed, T-D3 equivalent, re-pinned P-M17 killed) all show zero census kill, and the arm-deletion T-D4 co-fires the census pair by construction.\n14|- STATUS: Ready for review, handed off to review (review/integration are orchestrator steps).\n15|\n16|### 2253 — review round 4: parse-gate edges pinned behaviourally, census-only kills closed (F1a/F1b)\n(more lines below)"}}}
